{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 139, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-output edge with a residual shortcut gives large gains (exps 22, 26, 28), unlike overwriting an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the 0->3 conv with a skip often removes the cell's main or only conv, which hurts badly (exps 24, 25, 27)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is absent, edge 3 is often the only route from input to output, so deleting it collapses the network (exp 2)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 0 hurts more when it removes a 3x3 conv than when it removes a skip or pool (exps 84, 87, 90 vs 82, 86)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pruning a parameter-free skip on edge 1 is harmless or even helpful, whereas pruning a conv there loses capacity (exps 54, 56 vs 51, 59)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a skip on edge 5 costs little or helps in skip-heavy cells, while removing a conv on edge 5 hurts (exps 75, 77 vs 71, 72)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for a pool on edge 4 loses capacity, while swapping out a skip or an empty edge is near-neutral (exps 46, 47, 50 vs 42, 43)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip-dominated cells lack convolutions, so adding a 3x3 conv on edge 5 yields huge gains (exps 16, 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 1 is a skip the cell tends to be conv-poor, so adding a conv on edge 0 helps much more (exps 35, 36, 40 vs 31-34)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pool-dominated cells gain greatly from any learnable conv on the output edge (exps 95, 96 vs 91, 99, 100)."}], "tok": 32046, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"